<p>
  The main components of the app are <strong>Issues</strong> and <strong>Tasks</strong>.
  Issues are similar to GitHub issues. Anyone with access can use them to report bugs,
  suggest improvements, or ask a question. On the other hand, tasks can only be created by
  <strong>Reviewers</strong> or <strong>Admins</strong>. Often times, they are created
  from an Issue. They lay out specific instructions on how to fix the Issues' bugs or
  complete their new features. Tasks can also be added independently.
</p>

<h3>Type Configuration</h3>

<p>
  Issues and Tasks are grouped by <strong>types</strong> (eg. Bug, Feature Request,
  Question). <strong>Admins</strong> have several color and icon options available in
  order to customize their tags:
</p>

<h4>Color and Icon Options</h4>
<div class="issue-tags">
  <%= type_color_options %>
</div>

<h4>Icon Options</h4>
<div class="issue-tags">
  <%= type_icon_options %>
</div>

<h4>Priority Levels</h4>
<p>
  Tasks have a priority level assigned to them that indicate the importance of the bug
  fix, improvement, or new feature. The options are 1 to 4. Here is the quick guide
  of the levels and how they can be used:
</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Critical</strong> - Most likely tied to a bug that effects many users or clients</li>
  <li><strong>High</strong> - An important bug fix or new improvement</li>
  <li><strong>Medium</strong> - A new feature or improvement</li>
  <li><strong>Low</strong> - A new feature or improvement that can wait</li>
</ol>
